   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Split the term into partial fractions: \\( \\frac{4}{\\left(n + 3\\right) \\left(n + 4\\right)} = 4\\left(\\frac{1}{n + 3} - \\frac{1}{n + 4}\\right) \\).",
         "rule_named": "partial fractions"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "In the partial sum from \\( n = 3 \\) to \\( n = N \\) the middle terms cancel: \\( S_N = 4\\left(\\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{N + 4}\\right) \\).",
         "rule_named": "telescoping partial sum"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "As \\( N \\to \\infty \\), the second fraction approaches 0, so the value of the series is \\( \\frac{2}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            2,
